### Backend API Routes & Server

#### [NEW] [apiRouter.js](file:///c:/Users/Haree/OneDrive/Desktop/hck.1/server/apiRouter.js)
- Express router exporting the endpoints:
  - `POST /api/scan`: Parses `{ text, language, imageUrl }`, executes threat engine, saves to SQLite, and returns comprehensive verdict.
  - `GET /api/reports`: Returns all stored scan reports for the I4C admin dashboard.
  - `POST /api/reports/:id/report-i4c`: Flags `reportedToI4C = true` and updates timestamp.
  - `GET /api/health`: Health check endpoint.

#### [NEW] [index.js](file:///c:/Users/Haree/OneDrive/Desktop/hck.1/server/index.js)
- Standalone Express server running on port 5000 with CORS and JSON body parser.

#### [MODIFY] [vite.config.js](file:///c:/Users/Haree/OneDrive/Desktop/hck.1/vite.config.js)
- Integrates the API router as dev server middleware directly in Vite.
- When running `npm run dev`, API endpoints `/api/*` are handled immediately without requiring separate terminal management, while also providing proxy fallback if a standalone backend is running.

#### [MODIFY] [package.json](file:///c:/Users/Haree/OneDrive/Desktop/hck.1/package.json)
- Add dependencies `express` and `cors`.
- Add scripts: `"server": "node server/index.js"` and `"start": "node server/index.js"`.

